## Complete User Flows

### Flow A: First Video (New User)

```
1. User lands on Dashboard
   └─→ Sees empty state: "Create your first video"
   
2. Clicks "Create Pipeline" or "Use Template"
   └─→ Goes to Pipeline Editor with default template loaded
   
3. Clicks "Run Pipeline" button
   └─→ PRE-RUN MODAL opens (this is the key missing piece)
   
4. In Pre-Run Modal:
   ├─→ Step 1: Enter topic ("Top 10 AI Tools in 2024")
   ├─→ Step 2: Select archetype (Listicle, Tutorial, etc.)
   ├─→ Step 3: Quick settings (voice, duration, publish mode)
   ├─→ Step 4: Review cost estimate
   └─→ Click "Start Run"
   
5. Redirected to Run View
   └─→ Watch pipeline execute with live progress
   
6. Pipeline pauses at Script node
   └─→ INTERVENTION MODAL opens
   ├─→ User reviews generated script
   ├─→ Can edit inline, regenerate, or approve
   └─→ Clicks "Approve & Continue"
   
7. Pipeline continues through Voice, Thumbnail, Assembly
   └─→ May pause again for thumbnail selection
   
8. Pipeline reaches Publish
   └─→ Shows preview, asks for final confirmation
   └─→ User confirms, video publishes to YouTube
   
9. Success! 
   └─→ Shows YouTube link, stats, cost breakdown
```

